Z||000000||mikemace||03-20-2001||08:32 AM||||HELP! My right headlight was stuck open. I turned the manual knob on top of the motor and the light started working. The only problem is the motor would keep running ALL THE TIME!!! I unplugged the wires from the relay with the light in the up position. Does this sound like a relay problem?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||03-20-2001||09:08 AM||||Sounds like a gear inside the motor might be stripped.  You can disconnect the motor for now by unplugging the single wire connector.  Looks like you need a rebuild kit or try to find one in a boneyard.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  sells a rebuild kits.<P>Good info here on how to rebuild the motor:<BR><A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html</A><P>BTW, Welcome to the forum.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mikemace||03-20-2001||09:17 AM||||Thanks! I'm ordering the rebuild kits.||||reg||7
